// Mono-space font required
{
// Build special units when enemy_metal*ratio*income_mult*density_mult > team_response_metal
//   enemy_metal = the whole enemy team's seen units of the vs role; team_response_metal = finished mobile units of the
//   role from this AI and all its allies (humans too, refreshed every 2 s). max_percent still caps this AI's own army
//   density_mult = "density_curve" at the map player density = shortest side * 0.5 * longest side / allied team size,
//   sides in map units (16x16 etc.): 16x16 1v1 = 128, 8x8 5v5 = 6.4. Linear between points, first/last value outside.
//   Smaller = less response. Alone on the ally team (1v1, FFA) it is always 1. A role's own "density_curve"
//   overrides the shared one. Replaces eps_step
//
// Optional per role (all off when missing):
//   "density_curve": [[density, mult], ...]  replaces the shared density_curve for this role
//   "income_curve": [[income, mult], ...]  scales the amount of the role wanted (income_mult above), linear between
//       points, first/last value outside them. 0 = no response at that income (tier weights may still pick it)
//   "territory_max": 0.6  not built while ally mexes / map spots > this
//   "unlock_after": {"income": 25, "territory": 0.3}  locked until both are exceeded at once, then unlocked for good.
//       A missing or 0 field counts as met. Its income leaves out reclaim (ZK mex + overdrive + constructor share)
//   territory_max and unlock_after keep the role out of the response roll and the factory's tier-weight roll (unless
//   they would leave the factory nothing to build). Changes must hold 3 samples in a row (2 s apart, ~4 s).
//   Income = min(metal, energy) income * economy ecoFactor (the economy.json eps_step), as factory.json income_tier.
//   Gate luxury roles (artillery, heavy, super, transport), not counters (anti_air, riot, anti_heavy): a gate on a
//   counter stops it when the AI is behind and needs it most
// AA condition for 3v3: (enemy_air_metal*0.67 > (aa_metal+aa_cost)*1.12) and (aa_metal+aa_cost < army_metal*0.5)
//
// Probability of UnitDef for AA role depends on income tier: (tierN[UnitDef]+_weight_)*enemy_air_metal/aa_metal*importance
// armjeth probability for tier 1: (0.00+10.00)*enemy_air_metal*600.0
